  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Per-model harness confounding: each model runs exclusively in its own harness (Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Grok Build), so cross-model rows compare (interface, model, harness) tuples rather than isolated model capability.",
    "Mixed OSWorld 2.0 comparison regimes: Table 1 places 0808 full-set runs alongside StateAct on 0624, Gemini/Kimi pre-0808 reports with unspecified task counts, and OpenAI's unranked offline subset (72.60%).",
    "Benchmark coverage limits: OSWorld 2.0 (0808) contains 108 tasks (single-run main results) and MacAgentBench tests only a 28-task UI-dependent subset rather than full macOS coverage.",
    "Application-level regressions on OSWorld 1.0: VS Code (23 tasks) regresses on 3 of 4 models (-10.1 pp GPT-5.4, -13.0 pp Gemini 3.8 Flash, -2.2 pp Claude Opus 5.5) and Thunderbird drops on Opus (-10.7 pp) and Grok (-6.7 pp).",
    "Evaluated vs. Released build split: Section 4 main experiments and ablations ran the evaluated build (32-step cap, assert_ax), whereas the released build (64-step cap, unified wait/settle, zoom, JSON prefix) was evaluated only with GPT-5.4 in Appendix A.",
    "Security and local verification scope: cross-channel prompt-injection resilience across shared shell/AX/GUI sessions is untested, and this close reading did not re-execute the VM benchmarks locally."
  ],
